Z||000004||rockcrawl||08-26-2000||09:21 AM||||The Team Python site is the most informative I've found, and the guys are helpful too. Also check Chris West of West Coast Fiero. I'm doing a 4.9 in a Ferrari replica, but it's much different than a Fiero, so not much help. I used the entire Cad cradle and suspension mounted to a custom tubular frame. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fer3_1.jpg">  <BR>The pic shows a cadi 4100HT, but I have a 4.9 that will replace it. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 08-26-2000).]||||reg||1
